## Core Principle
Always design/develop mobile-first. Start with mobile styles, enhance for larger screens using Tailwind breakpoints

## Tailwind Breakpoints
Mobile-first: Base (no prefix, <640px) → `sm:` (≥640px) → `md:` (≥768px) → `lg:` (≥1024px) → `xl:` (≥1280px) → `2xl:` (≥1536px)

## Patterns
**Layout**: `flex flex-col sm:flex-row` (column mobile, row desktop)
**Typography**: `text-xl sm:text-2xl md:text-3xl` (smaller to larger)
**Spacing**: `p-4 sm:p-6 md:p-8` (smaller to larger)
**Visibility**: `block sm:hidden` (mobile-only), `hidden sm:block` (desktop-only)
**Grid**: `grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3` (single to multiple columns)

## Component Examples
**Dialog**: `w-full h-full sm:w-auto sm:h-auto` (fullscreen mobile, centered desktop)
**Nav**: `flex-col sm:flex-row` with hamburger (`sm:hidden`) and horizontal menu (`hidden sm:flex`)

## Testing
Test mobile first (dev tools emulation), verify touch targets (≥44x44px), check text readability, test landscape

## Common Mistakes
❌ Desktop-first: `flex-row max-md:flex-col`
❌ Missing mobile base: `lg:flex lg:gap-4`
❌ Small touch targets: `w-6 h-6` buttons
